  abstract={In this paper, we propose an approach for transforming use case requirements into actor-oriented activity charts. In this approach, we first specify requirements using a relatively more formalized use case template. Next, we generate actor-oriented activity charts by identifying various interactions of an actor with the system and the events sequenced thereafter. The resulting activity charts can be useful in various software planning and development activities like release planning, test planning, execution and others.},
  keywords={Unified modeling language;Databases;Planning;Semantics;Software;Standards;Resource management;Use case modeling;UML activity diagram;model transformation;requirement specification},
  doi={10.1109/APSEC.2012.149},
